<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20the%20Netherlands.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of the Netherlands</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The North Sea flood kills 1,836 people and leads to the Delta Works</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/dilmun"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dilmun.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dilmun</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Danish expedition under P.V. Glob and Geoffrey Bibby begins excavations</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/hebrew"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hebrew.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hebrew</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Israel founds the Academy of the Hebrew Language</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-egypt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Egypt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Egypt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 18 June the monarchy is abolished and Egypt declared a republic, with Muhammad Naguib as president and Gamal Abdel Nasser as prime minister.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-bhutan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Bhutan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Bhutan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">King Jigme Dorji Wangchuck establishes a 130-member National Assembly, followed by a Royal Advisory Council (1965) and a Cabinet (1968).</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/inuit"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Inuit.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Inuit</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">In the High Arctic relocation the Canadian government moves 17 Inuit families from Inukjuak to Resolute and Grise Fiord</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/conservatism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Conservatism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Conservatism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Russell Kirk sets out his five canons of conservatism in The Conservative Mind</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/democratic-republic-of-vietnam"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Democratic%20Republic%20of%20Vietnam.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Democratic Republic of Vietnam</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Viet Minh Land Reform Law of 4 December opens the land reform, carried out until 1956</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Cambodia%20(1953-1970).png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Cambodia (1953-1970)</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Cambodia achieves independence from France under Norodom Sihanouk</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/northern-rhodesia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Northern%20Rhodesia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Northern Rhodesia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Northern Rhodesia joins the Federation of Rhodesia and Nyasaland against strong African opposition</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-dien-bien-phu"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Dien%20Bien%20Phu.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Dien Bien Phu</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Premier René Mayer names Henri Navarre to command French Union forces in Indochina</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-dien-bien-phu"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Dien%20Bien%20Phu.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Dien Bien Phu</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Operation Castor begins, and the French drop or fly 9,000 troops into Điện Biên Phủ over three days</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-dien-bien-phu"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Dien%20Bien%20Phu.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Dien Bien Phu</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The garrison of Lai Chau sets out for Điện Biên Phủ, and only 185 of its 2,100 men arrive by 22 December</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/book-of-kells"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Book%20of%20Kells.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Book of Kells</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Roger Powell rebound the manuscript in four volumes</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/prambanan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Prambanan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Prambanan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The reconstruction of the main Shiva temple was completed and inaugurated by President Sukarno</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/mau-mau-rebellion"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mau%20Mau%20rebellion.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mau Mau rebellion</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mau Mau militants attack Lari on the night of 25 to 26 March, and a retaliatory massacre follows</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/stalinism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Stalinism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Stalinism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Stalin dies on 5 March and de-Stalinization follows</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/trotskyism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Trotskyism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Trotskyism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Fourth International splits into two public factions over the theses of Michel Pablo</span></li></ul></section>
